# The OLD standalone menu editor (a root-level `editor/` folder using the
# service-role key) must never be deployed. It has since been deleted, but we keep
# this rule ANCHORED to the repo root (`/editor`) in case it ever reappears.
#
# CRITICAL: the leading slash is REQUIRED. An unanchored `editor` matches ANYTHING
# named editor anywhere — including `app/editor`, `app/api/editor` and
# `public/panels/editor` (the manager panel), which silently 404'd the manager
# panel on every Vercel deploy until this was anchored.
/editor

# ── Nothing below here is code, and none of it is served ──────────────────────
# It was ALL being uploaded on every deploy: ~26 MB, which is 27% of the repo, on a
# stack that genuinely exhausts its ~100-deploy daily cap. Not serving them was never
# the question — Next only serves `public/` — the cost is the upload on every build.
#
# Competitor research: 185 files of 2-4 MB screenshots, plus a macOS .app bundle.
/All_compitior_POs_INFO
# Owner-facing explainer docs, read on GitHub, not by the app.
/LEARN-MY-APP
# Design explorations whose chosen design has already shipped.
/access-designs
# The frozen pre-rewrite reference (the code snapshot is already gitignored).
/reference
# Engineering docs + plans. Read in the repo, never at runtime.
/docs
/*.md
!/README.md
/PROJECT-HANDOFF.pdf
# Test + sweep output
/test-results
/tests
/.claude
